            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "I want to stay somewhat close to the capability pattern of fine-tuning enablement by buffer and client id. It's an easier pattern to recognize and gives the user more flexibility. It also makes it simple for the user to check enabled status by using a client_config() helper in the plugin or checking the client table directly.\r\n\r\nSince I'm using vim.g and vim.b for global and buffer configuration, my thinking was to use the client tables as a stand-in for a \"vim.c\" table space, sticking with the broader Neovim pattern.",
            "commit_id": "8c32a65661e8b97786ae74eb9eb1ffff07ac8cf7",
            "created_at": "2026-10-16T02:01:14Z",
